<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Waiver Wire' }) %>
<%- include('partials/_live_stale') %>
<%
  const money0 = n => '$' + Math.round(Number(n || 0)).toLocaleString('en-US');
  const top = claims && claims.length ? claims[0] : null;
%>

<h1 class="page-title">📋 Waiver Wire
  <span class="sub" style="font-weight:600">what the wire adds — and what this tool cannot tell you</span></h1>

<%# Found 2026-08-15 (re-audit): /waivers/log, /waivers/override, /stream/log,
    /stream/override redirected to a "success" query param UNCONDITIONALLY —
    on the SAME line whether predledger.append() succeeded or threw. This page
    never even read that param (no banner existed either way, success or
    failure), so nothing here was actively lying to anyone — but the redirect
    itself was, and the next person who wired a success banner off it would
    have inherited a false-positive. Fixed at the source (member.js) and this
    is the banner that should have existed from the start: real failure,
    actually shown. %>
<% if (typeof captureError !== 'undefined' && captureError) { %>
  <div class="alert-banner" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem; border-color:rgba(176,0,32,.6)">
    <span class="tag">⚠</span><span>That didn't save. The claim/stream/override was NOT recorded to the
    ledger — try again, or note it manually for now.</span>
  </div>
<% } %>

<%# ── THE THING THIS PAGE MUST NOT PAPER OVER ──────────────────────────────────
    Our league runs PRIORITY waivers, not FAAB. Priority is a depleting resource:
    one good claim and you drop to the bottom. So the decision is never "is this
    player good" — it is "is he worth spending my CURRENT POSITION on, or do I
    hold for something better". That is a stopping problem.

    The engine does not model it. It prices what a claim adds to the starting
    lineup, which is the NUMERATOR of the stopping rule and not the rule. A
    ranked list presented as the answer would be answering a question nobody
    asked, and the one thing worse than a tool that cannot decide is a tool that
    looks like it did. So the gap leads, once, and is not repeated. ────────── %>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem; border-left:3px solid var(--gold)">
  <div class="body">
    <p style="margin:0"><b>This tool prices the player. It does not decide the claim.</b></p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:.45rem 0 0; font-size:.86rem">
      We run <b>priority waivers</b>, so a claim costs your position in the order and one good
      claim drops you to the bottom. The real question is <i>“is he worth my current spot, or do
      I hold for something better”</i> — which depends on how many weeks are left, where you sit
      in the order, and what is likely to hit the wire later. <b>None of that is modelled here.</b>
      What is below is what each claim would add to your starting lineup, in points and dollars.
      Treat it as the number you weigh, not the answer.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<% if (err) { %>
  <div class="card"><div class="body"><p class="error-note">Couldn't read the wire: <%= err %></p></div></div>
<% } else if (!live) { %>
  <div class="card"><div class="body">
    <p style="margin:0"><b>No live roster yet.</b></p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:.4rem 0 0">
      The wire lights up once Sleeper has a roster and a slate — after the draft. Nothing to
      claim in August, and that is the correct answer rather than an empty table.
    </p>
  </div></div>
<% } else if (!top) { %>
  <%# THE NOTHING WEEK, SAID OUT LOUD. The engine returns a ranked list even when
      every entry is worth zero or less; a page that renders that list is
      manufacturing a recommendation. And on this one question the stopping rule
      IS decidable: a claim worth nothing is never worth a priority position. %>
  <div class="card lo-nochange"><div class="body">
    <p style="margin:0"><b>✅ Nothing on the wire improves your lineup this week.</b></p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:.45rem 0 0">
      Every available player scores at or below what you would have to drop, so no claim would
      put a single point on the field. <b>Hold your priority.</b> That is the one version of the
      stopping question this tool can answer on its own — a claim worth nothing is never worth
      your position in the order.
    </p>
  </div></div>
<% } else { %>
  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem">
    <h2>🔼 What the wire would add
      <span class="sub"><%= claims.length %> claim<%= claims.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %> that reach your lineup<% if (drop) { %> · you would drop <b><%= drop.name %></b><% } %></span></h2>
    <div class="body">
      <% claims.forEach((c, i) => { %>
        <div class="lo-call">
          <div class="lo-call-main">
            <span class="lo-start">▲ Claim <b><%= c.name %></b>
              <span class="muted">(<%= c.position %><% if (c.consensus_projection != null) { %>, <%= c.consensus_label %> <%= c.consensus_projection %><% } %>)</span></span>
            <span class="lo-sit">▼ drop <b><%= c.drop ? c.drop.name : '—' %></b>
              <span class="muted"><%= c.why %></span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="lo-call-price">
            <%# POINTS FIRST. Dollars are modelled — they run through the weekly-high
                band and an opponent estimate. Points are the number you can check
                against your own lineup, which is what makes this auditable. %>
            <span class="lo-dollars money-up">+<%= c.net_value.toFixed(1) %> pts</span>
            <span class="lo-split muted"><%= money0(c.dollars) %> at <%= perPoint.toFixed(2) %>/pt</span>
          </div>
          <%# CONTESTED IS SHOWN AND EXPLICITLY NOT PRICED. The engine computes who
              else is short at the position and then values the claim identically
              whether three teams want him or nobody does. In a PRIORITY league
              that is backwards — contested is when spending your spot is
              justified, uncontested is when you can wait — so the fact is
              surfaced with the caveat attached rather than folded into a number
              that would then be wrong. %>
          <div class="lo-note" style="grid-column:1/-1; margin-top:.35rem">
            <%# POSTURE IS NOT KNOWN, SO IT IS NOT CLAIMED.
                This line first read "including N contending or desperate", and
                that was false the moment it rendered: the route computes no
                postures, whoElseNeeds defaults a missing posture to eager (a
                sensible CONSERVATIVE default inside the engine), and the page
                turned that unknown into a statement about nine teams' competitive
                state. Absent is not a value. What IS established is the count of
                teams with an open startable slot at the position, so that is all
                that is said. %>
            <% const known = c.rivals.filter(r => r.posture); %>
            <% if (c.contested) { %>
              <b style="color:#d4242f">⚔ <%= c.rivals.length %> other team<%= c.rivals.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %></b>
              <%= c.rivals.length === 1 ? 'has' : 'have' %> an open <%= c.position %> slot<% if (known.length) { %>, <%= known.length %> of them contending or desperate<% } %>.
              <span class="muted">Whether they would actually spend their priority on him is <b>not modelled</b>. And it is <b>not in the dollar figure above</b> — the price is the same whether he is contested or not.</span>
            <% } else { %>
              <span class="muted">No other team has an open <%= c.position %> slot. He may still be there next week — which is the case for holding, and again, not priced above.</span>
            <% } %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% }) %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>What you would be spending</h2>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin:0">
        The best claim is worth <b><%= top.net_value.toFixed(1) %> points</b> (<%= money0(top.dollars) %>) for one week of your lineup.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.5rem 0 0; font-size:.86rem">
        Against that you are spending a waiver position you get back slowly, and this tool has no
        model of what the rest of the season puts on the wire. If you want the stopping rule
        properly — claim when the value beats what you would expect to see before your priority
        recovers — that needs the arrival distribution of wire talent, and it is not built.
        It is written up in <code>LEARNING-ARCHITECTURE.md</code> §1 as buildable, and until it
        exists this page is deliberately one number short of a decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Log the decision (writes to the ledger with its counterfactual) ─────
      Same pattern as /lineup/log + /lineup/override: two forms, one records
      agreement with the tool's own alternative as the counterfactual, the
      other records going another way with the tool's pick AS the
      counterfactual. This page has no "submit the claim" action of its own
      (the real claim happens on Sleeper) so this tap IS the decision moment -
      it says "this is what I'm doing", not just "this is what I saw". %>
  <form method="post" action="/waivers/log" class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem">
    <div class="body" style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap">
      <div>
        <b>Making this claim?</b>
        <span class="muted" style="font-size:.82rem">Logs it against holding your priority, so the rest of the season can grade the difference.</span>
      </div>
      <input type="hidden" name="week" value="<%= weekNo || '' %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="dollars" value="<%= top.dollars %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="contested" value="<%= top.contested ? '1' : '0' %>">
      <%# double-escape bug fixed 2026-08-15 — see lineup.ejs's note by the same fix
          for the full mechanism. Was .replace(/"/g,'&quot;') stacked on EJS's own
          output escaping, so a real browser submitted unparseable text instead of JSON. %>
      <input type="hidden" name="chosen" value="<%= JSON.stringify({ id: top.player_id, name: top.name, pos: top.position, net_value: top.net_value }) %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="drop" value="<%= JSON.stringify(top.drop || {}) %>">
      <button class="btn gold" type="submit">Log this claim</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <form method="post" action="/waivers/override" class="card lo-override" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem">
    <div class="body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:.55rem">
        <b>Holding, or claiming someone else?</b>
        <span class="muted" style="font-size:.82rem">One tap says why. The tool's pick was worth <b><%= money0(top.dollars) %></b>.</span>
      </div>
      <input type="hidden" name="week" value="<%= weekNo || '' %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="dollars" value="<%= top.dollars %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="recommended" value="<%= JSON.stringify({ id: top.player_id, name: top.name, pos: top.position, net_value: top.net_value }) %>">
      <div class="lo-ov-chips">
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="held priority">✋ Held priority</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="claimed someone else">🔀 Claimed someone else</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="injury news">🏥 Injury news</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="don't buy the projection">📉 Don't buy the projection</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="unstated">Just record it</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.55rem 0 0; font-size:.74rem">
        What you actually claimed is readable from Sleeper afterwards. What the tool told you
        <i>right now</i> isn't recoverable from anything, so that's what gets written down.
      </p>
    </div>
  </form>
<% } %>

<%# ── STREAMING (K/DEF) — independent of the claims block above: a stream can
    be worth doing even in a week with no priority claim worth spending, and
    vice versa. Same evaluateClaims ranking as the claims above, filtered to
    K/DEF, HONESTLY LABELLED as season-value rather than matchup-tuned — no
    new scoring logic was built for this, on purpose. %>
<% if (live && !err && streamClaims && streamClaims.length) { %>
  <% const s = streamClaims[0]; %>
  <% const holding = (currentKD || []).find(p => p.position === s.position); %>
  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem; border-left:3px solid var(--gold)">
    <h2>🔁 Streaming (<%= s.position %>)
      <span class="sub">season-value ranking, not matchup-tuned — a real limit, not hidden</span></h2>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin:0">
        <b><%= s.name %></b> ranks <%= s.net_value.toFixed(1) %> pts above
        <% if (holding) { %> your current <%= s.position %>, <b><%= holding.name %></b><% } else { %> what you're currently starting<% } %>
        for this week — <%= money0(s.dollars) %>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.5rem 0 0; font-size:.82rem">
        This is the same season-value model as the claims above, not a matchup read (no
        opponent-defense or weather signal is built into it yet). A stream costs no waiver
        priority — the alternative here is simply keeping who you already have, not holding
        a position in line.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <form method="post" action="/stream/log" class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem">
    <div class="body" style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap">
      <div><b>Streaming this?</b>
        <span class="muted" style="font-size:.82rem">Logs it against who you already have, so the season can grade the difference.</span></div>
      <input type="hidden" name="week" value="<%= weekNo || '' %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="dollars" value="<%= s.dollars %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="chosen" value="<%= JSON.stringify({ id: s.player_id, name: s.name, pos: s.position, net_value: s.net_value }) %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="counterfactual" value="<%= JSON.stringify(holding || { note: 'no current ' + s.position + ' on roster' }) %>">
      <button class="btn gold" type="submit">Log this stream</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <form method="post" action="/stream/override" class="card lo-override" style="margin-bottom:1.1rem">
    <div class="body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:.55rem"><b>Not streaming?</b>
        <span class="muted" style="font-size:.82rem">One tap says why.</span></div>
      <input type="hidden" name="week" value="<%= weekNo || '' %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="dollars" value="<%= s.dollars %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="recommended" value="<%= JSON.stringify({ id: s.player_id, name: s.name, pos: s.position, net_value: s.net_value }) %>">
      <%# WHAT DECLINING THE STREAM ACTUALLY MEANS (2026-08-15): keeping the
          K/DEF already rostered — the same `holding` object the log form above
          records as its counterfactual. Captured so the override is gradeable:
          the kept player's real week vs the recommended stream's real week. %>
      <input type="hidden" name="actual" value="<%= JSON.stringify(holding || { note: 'no current ' + s.position + ' on roster' }) %>">
      <div class="lo-ov-chips">
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="kept current">✋ Kept who I have</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="streamed someone else">🔀 Streamed someone else</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="don't buy the projection">📉 Don't buy the projection</button>
        <button class="btn small ghost" type="submit" name="reason" value="unstated">Just record it</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>
<% } %>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
